WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.890
- Hello everyone, I'm Asa Waldstein,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.570
and I'm here today with some lessons

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.310
about labeling compliance.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.670
Labeling of dietary
supplements is very important

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.010
because if a label
format is not correctly,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.290
this can really signal to the authorities

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.440
THAT THERE MIGHT BE DEEPER GMP ISSUES.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.330
So this warning letter came from

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.830
of a company being inspected.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.140
During that inspection, the FDA,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.020
issued several 483s to the company

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.120
and they also collected
a lot of product labels.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.310
So really, I think the reason why

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.040
this company received
the warning letter rather

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.150
because of their improper 483 response.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.060
And I talk more about 483 responses

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.500
and the differences between

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.400
a 483 and a warning letter
is in a previous post,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.920
and I'll drop a link to to
that here in the comments.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.570
SO THE KEY LEARNING POINTS TODAY

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.190
have to do with label compliance.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.220
SO, LET'S REALLY DIG IN
ON WHAT WE CAN LEARN.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.500
So, a common mistake
I see companies making

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.450
is with supplement fact panels

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.460
not matching the suggested use.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.040
For example, if the suggested use says,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.470
"take 1-2 capsules daily"

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.870
the supplement fact panel should list

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.790
the higher amount consumed
at one time (2 caps).

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.490
So if it says "take 1-2 capsules daily"

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.460
you must write the higher
number (two capsules).

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.910
And according to the FDA,

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:19.470
the serving amount is the
amount consumed at one time.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.800
So if you write, "take one
capsule three times a day",

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.480
the serving size is one.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.110
If you write, "take one to two
capsules three times a day",

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.990
the serving size would be that
higher number, which is two.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.850
So also in this warning letter

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.370
it notes the incorrect listing of items

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.150
with the daily value percentage,
such as pantothenic acid.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.220
So the FDA has pretty strict rules

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.290
on how you list different items

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.330
with daily value percentages such as

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.740
calcium, magnesium

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.460
niacin, folate, and pantothenic acid.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.510
So in this warning letter,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.030
the company was cited for not listing

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.650
a lot of the B vitamins correctly.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.310
They wrote "vitamin B1"
instead of "thiamin"

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.700
and they wrote "vitamin B5"
instead of "pantothenic acid".

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.130
So it's really important
to make sure that you're

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.230
listing products in your
supplement fact panel

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.640
in the correct format.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.280
The American Herbal
Products Association (AHPA)

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.410
has a wonderful labeling guidance,

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.470
but I do believe this is only
available for members now.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.303
Also, I use ESHA's

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.136
Dietary Supplement Fact Panel Program,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.590
which is really good too.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.423
It's kind of pricey,

00:02:23.423 --> 00:02:25.440
but it's well worth the
money in my opinion,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.350
and I use it every week
in my consulting practice.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.080
And the FDA also has a decent resource

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.090
for the order of ingredients,

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.530
and I'll make sure that link

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.320
is included in the Warning
Letter Wednesday post.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.410
So other learning lessons have
to do with label formatting.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.350
So, companies are probably not
going to get a warning letter

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.200
if the labels are not formatted correctly.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.840
But again, where there's
smoke there is fire,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.730
if the labels aren't laid out correctly

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.020
and formatted correctly,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.910
this can really signal to the authorities

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.460
that there might be deeper GMP problems

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.430
if the manufacturer doesn't know the rule,

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.980
the basics of labeling,
what else don't they know?

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.890
So it can really signal the
authorities to look deeper.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.660
So some other key lessons,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.460
not necessarily from this warning letter,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.040
but in general have to do
with the line thickness.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.260
So the FDA has several

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.810
supplement fact panel
examples on their website,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.723
and I'll throw one up on the
screen here for you to see.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.680
You can see there's a certain
type of line thickness

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.270
underneath Supplement Facts

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.720
and before "percent daily
Vvalues not not established".

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.480
So again, the FDA wants these

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.570
supplement fact panels to be
laid out in the correct format.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.780
There are so many more
labeling potential issues

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.400
so please feel free to reach out to me

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.600
with your labeling questions.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.730
I'm more than happy to
set up a free consult

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.410
to discuss labeling needs.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.700
Once again, I'm Asa Waldstein.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.533
Have a great day!

